{"kind":"request","text":"CB-1 pre-code proposal at main 4cef11d2. No code or executable validation.\n\nOrder stays after the cutover deployment and AE-1. Ruling 657e4217 makes NF-7 a hosted witness after NF-5 lands and the planner deploys it. NF-7 no longer requires an earlier CB-1 or a local Counter browser adapter.\n\n1. Current blockers and their owners\n\nThe engine already contains base: packages/platform/src/base-cohort.ts pins Register 28, Directory 27, Membership 14, Rules 15, Destination 21 and Inbox 1. packages/scope/src/creation-versions.ts admits the newest base pins even when an explicit creation policy adds historical pins. I found no celld-specific evaluator restriction that requires rewriting these definitions.\n\napps/room/celld/mac/prepare-project.mjs rejects base through celldPreparedNoHostRegister. packages/platform/src/version-questions.ts admits only Register 21 and 25 for that question, and only Register 21 for celldSmokeOwnedPlanRegister. scripts/celld-smoke.mjs explicitly plans --cohort unpublished and refuses other retained plans. The prepare-project test explicitly expects base refusal. These choices keep the old family and account for the missing Native member/key/agent behavior, ordinary v2 capability admission, failed-claim state and fixed read-token rule listed in docs/self-host-mac.md. Those features already exist in base. They do not each need a new celld port.\n\napps/room/celld/wrangler.json omits APPLICATION_CONTENT and APPLICATION_TRUST. packages/scope/src/applications/wiring.ts refuses unsupported-host without the content binding; the production admission path also needs exact release/publisher/host trust. apps/room/celld/mac/deploy.py requires every non-vars config field to equal the maintained template and admits only enumerated vars. prepare-github.mjs enforces the same shape before adding GitHub settings. Thus an operator cannot stage the missing package binding/trust through the normal helpers by editing private output. This is a preparation/deployment allowlist gap, not a reason to replace ApplicationContentStore.\n\napps/room/worker.ts has no archive wiring. worker.grow.ts and apps/room/archive.ts wire the current Grow-only driver, and archive-policy.ts admits its fixed policies. AE-1 owns their replacement with the shared driver and package/platform policy discovery. CB-1 must consume that driver after it lands.\n\nThe local archive provider remains a distinct gap. apps/room/celld/wrangler.json has no ARTIFACTS binding or host settings, and celld does not offer Cloudflare Artifacts. packages/scope/src/github-host.ts says “No production archive mint” and exposes only fixtureArchive(ports). packages/scope/src/artifacts-host.ts has the present production archive provider. Merely admitting Directory 27 or recording archive:journal cannot create a production GitHub exporter.\n\ndocs/self-host-mac.md, docs/celld.md and docs/hosts.md describe the historical default and limits. They must describe base, explicit retained old plans, package settings, repository state and the actual archive provider. The historical journals keep their pins.\n\n2. Host needs and --host none\n\nFounding --host none records no namespace or repository. It needs the normal Worker/session/index/creation wiring, not Git credentials. Base member/key/agent rules and failed-claim judgments do not acquire a host dependency.\n\nOrdinary package installation needs a public immutable package Git URI, the exact trust row on the Worker and CLI, and APPLICATION_CONTENT. packages/scope/src/worker.ts routes fetch/admit application operations independently of the repository host, so a host-none room can install Counter through the normal CLI. The fleet object bucket does not itself become an archive or package binding.\n\nnotes/2026-10-19-self-hosting-on-celld.md §4.3 specifies celld r2_buckets over the fleet bucket, with APPLICATION_CONTENT bucket_name application-content and prefix r2/application-content/. It also states that every R2 method fails without a fleet bucket. notes/implementation/2026-10-19-celld-qualification.md says its runs did not install a package. Therefore this proposal uses the persistent Mac fleet with its S3 store, not celld dev, and still owes a real package-store witness.\n\nDirectory 27 reserves declared prefixes and tells its Destination the application-paths row even before a repository exists. Prefixes constrain authority; they do not supply a Git host. Destination retains the inherited no-repository guards on publication, so --host none cannot push files. Once a valid repository is bound, the same recorded prefix restrictions still apply.\n\nWith no repository, bind-archive must refuse no-repository. Base-directory.ts fixes the old wrong-item lookup; it does not make a null repository archiveable. AE-1 explicitly requires a host-none room to have no archive and its pages to say so. The base family permits a later GitHub binding, but the positive archive scene needs a bound repository plus the shared driver and a real production provider. A binding receipt alone proves no exported bytes.\n\n3. Proposed change and normal local witness\n\nKeep prepare-project as an offline consumer of the retained plan. Change the normal plan producer in scripts/celld-smoke.mjs to the base default and admit Register 28 in the two explicit celld version questions. Preserve explicit historical plan support. Add bounded private staging and validation for APPLICATION_CONTENT r2_buckets and APPLICATION_TRUST across prepare-project, prepare-github and deploy.py. Use the existing ApplicationContentStore and production HTTP packet transport unchanged. Add only the approved post-AE-1 archive configuration and provider wiring to the Mac staging/deployment path. Do not copy Grow's driver or add a fixture port.\n\nAfter the planner accepts the provider decision and AE-1 lands, use the pinned runtime as a persistent local Mac fleet with the normal S3 store and HTTPS proxy in docs/self-host-mac.md. Retain a fresh private CLI home and plan. Prepare/deploy base through the normal helpers, finish install, create a room, join a member and verify the platform journals. Stage exact trust and the package R2 binding. The member installs the normal public Counter packet with dap install \u003cimmutable-GitURI\u003e --release \u003crelease\u003e --request \u003ckept-key\u003e. Read its recorded active install and verify the actual application journal. Restart/redeploy the fleet and confirm the stored package bytes still load. This is CLI/package coverage; the installed-screen browser witness remains NF-7's hosted obligation.\n\nBefore repository binding, witness prefix reservation and refusal of repository publication and archive binding. Then use the normal GitHub App staging and bind-repository path for the same base room, let Directory observe the binding, and send bind-archive as owner. The positive archive witness must use the selected production provider. Clone with dap clone \u003cdir\u003e --archive and replay --all --expect-journals N --json, where N comes from a separate scope inventory that includes Counter. Preserve public result evidence and keep keys, session secrets and Git tokens private. Run focused changed tests and the gate only in the root's later execution slot.\n\nPlanner decisions before CB-1 source:\nA. Accept the persistent Mac fleet + R2 package path and the base-default plan/preparation proposal, with celld dev excluded from the package witness.\nB. Which production archive provider should complete the local scene? I recommend the existing normal GitHub binding path, but it has no production archive mint today. Does AE-1 own adding that provider so CB-1 only stages it, or should a separate host item supply it before CB-1? I will not substitute fixtureArchive, a fake Artifacts binding, or a new self-host Git service.\nC. Confirm the archive scene means a room founded under --host none that later binds GitHub. An unchanged host-none room must retain no-repository and no archive under AE-1.","body":{"conditions":"Accept or amend the CB-1 pre-code proposal and decide the normal local archive provider, its work-item owner, and the post-binding scene before CB-1 source edits.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}